 Since we want $n$ F's, the other $10-n$  questions must be T's.  Thus, we must choose from the $10$ questions i.e. $\binom{10}{n}$ to be F's, then the number of ways is simply this:
\begin{align*}
S= 1+\binom{10}{1}+\binom{10}{2}+\binom{10}{3}+\cdots + \binom{10}{10} = 2^{10}-1-10-45 = \boxed{964}
\end{align*}

